<title>TUNISIA: Lower Tunisian current account deficit expected.</title>
<headline>Lower Tunisian current account deficit expected.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisia's current account deficit for 1996 is estimated at 685.6 million dinars or 3.6 percent of gross domestic product (GDP), compared with 785 million dinars or 4.4 percent of GDP in 1995, a draft government budget report showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The draft, obtained by Reuters, forecasts the current account deficit will fall further in 1997 to 616.2 million dinars or 2.9 percent of GDP.</p>
<p>($=0.98 dinar)</p>
<p>Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
